meta {
  name: browser pane status
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/browser/status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~sessionId: {{sessionId}}
}

docs {
  Whether a native browser pane is attached (desktop shell) and what THIS session's browser is showing: {attached, url}. url is null without a sessionId — a page that has not started a session has no browser and no address. On the web face attached:false is the honest answer, not an error.
  
  Fence: host+origin — Loopback fence plus Origin check: an Origin header, if present, must be loopback. REST clients send no Origin header, which counts as safe — requests pass. A manually added foreign Origin answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
